# Dashboard — desktop only

The **Daros dashboard** (`/dashboard`) must run only on **desktop computers** (laptops/desktops).

## Product rule

- **Allow:** desktop browsers (fine pointer, no phone/tablet UA).
- **Block:** phones, tablets, and touch-first devices (including iPad with desktop UA).

## Implementation

- Detection: `src/lib/device/handheldDetection.ts` (`isHandheldDevice`, `getHandheldStorePlatform`).
- Gate UI: `DashboardMobileGate` — mobile app in development; show **App Store** (iOS/iPadOS) or **Google Play** (Android).
- Wrap **`/signin`** and **`/dashboard`** with `HandheldWebGate` in `App.tsx`.
- Marketing CTAs: `HandheldAuthLink` on Sign In buttons (Navbar, Hero, etc.) sends handheld users to `/signin` (gate).

Do **not** remove the gate or add responsive “mobile dashboard” layouts without an explicit product change. Marketing pages (`/`, marketing routes) stay accessible on mobile; **sign-in and dashboard are not**.

When adding new authenticated app shells, reuse `DashboardDesktopOnly` or the same detection helpers.
